commit 162dc276a85b4f7d353adbe312d05d8e7a4c28e3
Author: Christopher Cameron <ccameron@google.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 22 11:33:45 2026 -0700

    media: Support IT35 metadata tracks in FFmpegDemuxer
    
    Add the kFFmpegDemuxerIT35MetadataTrack feature flag to control this
    behavior (disabled by default), and add unit tests for MP4 files with
    cdsc and rndr track references.
    
    Add a structure MetadataTrackEntry for each metadata track (created
    using the static function BuildMetadataTracks). When metadata samples
    arrive, route them using CacheMetadataPacket.
    
    In FFmpegDemuxerStream::SatisfyPendingRead, before passing the
    DecoderBuffers on, first ensure that their metadata has been attached
    using the function PrepareFrontBufferForRead, which calls back into the
    demuxer to attach the metadata. This will not submit buffers until they
    are ready or until we have already read too far (2 seconds) ahead
    without finding the metadata.
    
    Leave handling of seeking for a future patch (as a TODO).
    
    Bug: 480162031
    Change-Id: I5c4c1e43745b7bcd91373101fa446f60389d781d
